  "description": "GUHQOR crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P 1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C54 H115 Cr3 Ho3 N3 O25 2+,1.5(C2 H3 N1),2.5(H2 O1),2(Cl1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr2 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr3 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho5 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho6 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Cr4 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr5 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr6 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.301-3.955 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.85-112.28°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [C54H115Cr3Ho3N3O25]2+·2Cl−·1.5MeCN·2.5H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Explicit bracketed charge: 2+.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
